  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...The long term forecast \nremains largely uneventful as an area of ridging persists over \nthe gulf through Saturday, bringing northwesterly flow, drier \nconditions, and warmer temperatures through the second half of the\nweek. The whole panhandle will see clear skies through Friday, \nwith cloud cover moving in from the north starting Saturday. \nNortherly winds will increase up to 25 mph overnight Wednesday and\nthrough Thursday. Winds will decrease again overnight into Friday\nmorning before the flow switches southerly through the afternoon \nas the pressure gradient turns. Through the weekend, southerly \nwinds in Lynn Canal will increase to around 20 kts with the help \nof sea breezes through midday. Other communities should also feel \nlocal sea breezes increase midday. High temperatures will reach \nthe high 60s to low 70s in the northern panhandle and into the 70s\nin the southern panhandle Thursday and Friday with ample \nclearing. Some areas in the southern panhandle are looking like \nthey may reach the upper 70s Friday and Saturday, mainly Hyder, so\nwill continue to watch that through the week. Models are still in\ndisagreement going into the weekend, with the EC holding onto the\nridge in the gulf and the GFS favoring an upper level shortwave \nmaking it over the ridge and into the northern panhandle \nmid weekend. Including a chance for rainfall in the northern \npanhandle through Saturday evening, increasing into Sunday. \nDepending on how things change over the next few days, we could \nhave a very dry or very wet weekend.",
